<h1>Prerequisites</h1>
<ul>
<li><a href=3D"https://www.pollfish.com/dashboard/dev/" target=3D"_blank">P=
rodege Publisher Account</a></li>
<li>Android API 21 or later</li>
<li>Java 1.8</li>
<li>Kotlin 1.9.0</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<h1>Quick Guide</h1>
<ol>
<li>Obtain a <a href=3D"https://www.pollfish.com/signup/publisher" target=
=3D"_blank">Publisher Account</a></li>
<li>Create a new App and copy the given API key</li>
<li>Create a new placement and copy the given placement id</li>
<li>Add Prodege SDK in your project</li>
<li>Initialize Prodge SDK</li>
<li>Load a Placement</li>
<li>Show the placement</li>
<li>Update you privacy policy and publish your app</li>
<li>Request your account to get verified</li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Apps designed for <a href=3D"https://play.google.=
com/about/families/ads-monetization/" target=3D"_blank">Children and Famili=
es program</a> should not be using Prodege SDK, since Prodege does not coll=
ect responses from users less than 16 years old.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><br></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Prodege SDK requires minSdk 21. If your app suppo=
rts a lower minSdk you can still build your app please refer to section 7.<=
/p>
</blockquote>
<h1>Analytical steps</h1>
<h2>1. Obtain a Publisher Account</h2>
<p>Register as a Publisher at <a href=3D"https://www.pollfish.com/signup/pu=
blisher" target=3D"_blank">www.pollfish.com</a></p>
<p><br></p>
<h2>2. Create a new App and copy the given API key</h2>
<p>Login at <a href=3D"https://www.pollfish.com/docs/www.pollfish.com/login=
/publisher" target=3D"_blank">www.pollfish.com</a> and click "Add a new app=
" on the <a href=3D"https://www.pollfish.com/dashboard/dev/" target=3D"_bla=
nk">Publisher Dashboard</a>. Copy then the given API key for this app in or=
der to use later on, when initializing Prodege SDK within your code.</p>
<p><br></p>
<h2>3. Create a new placement and copy the given placement id</h2>
<p>Navigate in your <a href=3D"https://www.pollfish.com/dashboard/dev/" tar=
get=3D"_blank">Publisher Dashboard</a> under App Settings - Placements and =
choose "Create a Placement". You can select a Rewarded Ad or an Offerwall a=
pproach based on your placement needs with any of the available Ad Formats(=
it can change later through placement settings). Hit "Create Placement" and=
 copy the generated Placement id in order to use later on.</p>
<p><br></p>
<h2>4. Add Prodege SDK in your project</h2>
<h3><strong>4.1. Retrieve Prodege Android SDK through maven</strong></h3>
<p>Retrieve Prodege SDK through <strong>maven()</strong> with gradle by add=
ing the following line in your app's module <strong>build.gradle</strong> f=
ile:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-groovy hljs">dependencies {
    implementation <span class=3D"hljs-string">'com.prodege:prodege:7.0.0-b=
eta07'</span>
}
</code></pre>
<p><br></p>
<h3><strong>4.2. Manual installation</strong></h3>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> If you are using Android Studio, right click on y=
our project and select New Module. Then select Import .JAR or .aar Package =
option and from the file browser locate the <code>.aar</code> file. Right c=
lick again on your project and in the Module Dependencies tab choose to add=
 the module that you recently added, as a dependency.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>4.2.1 Download Prodege Android SDK <code>.aar</code> file and import it=
 into your project's libraries</h3>
<p>Click <a href=3D"https://storage.googleapis.com/pollfish_production/sdk/=
Android/Prodege%20Android%20SDK-7.0.0-beta07.zip" target=3D"_blank">here</a=
> to download the latest version of Prodege SDK.</p>
<p><strong>For Java based projects</strong> you will have to include the Ko=
tlin runtime library in your module dependencies and set the java to versio=
n 1.8.</p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-groovy hljs">android {
    <span class=3D"hljs-comment">// ...</span>
   =20
    compileOptions {
        sourceCompatibility JavaVersion.VERSION_1_8
        targetCompatibility JavaVersion.VERSION_1_8
    }
}

dependencies {
    <span class=3D"hljs-comment">// ...</span>
   =20
    implemetation <span class=3D"hljs-string">'org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-=
stdlib:1.9.0'</span>
}
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Skipping this step will result to runtime excepti=
on during the SDK initialization.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><br></p>
<h3>4.2.2 Add Google Play Advertising Identifier library to your project (O=
ptional)</h3>
<p>Applications that integrate Prodege SDK may use Google Play Services lib=
rary in order to give access to the Advertising ID of a device to the SDK. =
Further details regarding integration with the Google Play services library=
 can be found <a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/android/guides/setup=
" target=3D"_blank">here</a>. By skipping this step you have to provide a u=
serId during initialization. Refer to section 6 for more details.</p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-groovy hljs">dependencies {
    implementation <span class=3D"hljs-string">'com.google.android.gms:play=
-services-ads-identifier:18.0.1'</span>
}
</code></pre>
<p><br></p>
<h3><strong>4.3. Add Advertising Id permission for Android 12+ (Optional if=
 manual installation without Google Play Advertising Identifier library int=
egration)</strong></h3>
<p>Apps updating their target API level to 31 (Android 12) or higher will n=
eed to declare a Google Play services normal permission in the AndroidManif=
est.xml file.</p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-xml hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;<span c=
lass=3D"hljs-title">uses-permission</span> <span class=3D"hljs-attribute">a=
ndroid:name</span>=3D<span class=3D"hljs-value">"com.google.android.gms.per=
mission.AD_ID"</span> /&gt;</span>
</code></pre>
<p>You can read more about Google Advertising ID changes <a href=3D"https:/=
/support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/6048248" target=3D"=
_blank">here</a>.</p>
<p><br></p>
<h3><strong>4.4. Add support for cleartext http traffic (Optional)</strong>=
</h3>
<p>If you are looking to use Prodege Mediation surveys from all the provide=
rs, in order to avoid any faulty behaviour on new Android devices we would =
advice that you allow cleartext http traffic for the following domains. To =
achieve that you need to:</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Donwload <a href=3D"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pollfish/andro=
id-sdk-pollfish/b94e812c8b61ad1ac72c16cd63892168c892a04c/resources/domain_w=
hitelist.xml" download=3D"" target=3D"_blank">
this file
</a> and place it under <strong><code>res/xml</code></strong> directory.</p=
></li>
<li><p>In your AndroidManifest.xml file add <strong><code>android:networkSe=
curityConfig</code></strong> tag as below:</p></li>
</ol>
<pre><code class=3D"language-xml hljs"> <span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;<span =
class=3D"hljs-title">application</span>
    <span class=3D"hljs-attribute">...</span>
    <span class=3D"hljs-attribute">android:networkSecurityConfig</span>=3D<=
span class=3D"hljs-value">"@xml/domain_whitelist"</span>&gt;</span>
</code></pre>
<p><br></p>
<h2>5. Initialize Prodege SDK</h2>
<p>In order to initialize Prodege SDK, you will need a <code>Context</code>=
 and the api key as provided by the <a href=3D"https://www.pollfish.com/das=
hboard/dev/" target=3D"_blank">Publisher Dashboard</a> in step 2. We advise=
 to call <code>Prodge.initialize</code> as soon as possible within your app=
lication's lifecycle, for example in the <code>onCreate()</code> mehod of y=
our <code>Application</code> or <code>Activity</code> class. This will init=
ialize Prodege SDK with default configuration. Read further for additional =
configuration options and notfications on the initialization result.</p>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration: underline">Kotlin:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-kotlin hljs">Prodege.initialize(context, <span=
 class=3D"hljs-string">"API_KEY"</span>)
</code></pre>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration: underline">Java:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-java hljs">Prodege.initialize(context, <span c=
lass=3D"hljs-string">"API_KEY"</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">null</s=
pan>, <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">null</span>);
</code></pre>
<p><br></p>
<h3><strong>5.1. Configure Prodege SDK initialization (Optional)</strong></=
h3>
<p>You can use any of the additional configuration options to control the b=
ehaviour of the Prodege SDK by creating an <code>InitOptions.Builder</code>=
 instance and build upon it.</p>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration: underline">Kotlin:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-kotlin hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">impo=
rt</span> com.prodege.builder.InitOptions

<span class=3D"hljs-variable"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">val</span> optio=
nsBuilder</span> =3D InitOptions.Builder()
</code></pre>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration: underline">Java:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-java hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import=
</span> com.prodege.builder.InitOptions;

InitOptions.Builder optionsBuilder =3D <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">new</sp=
an> InitOptions.Builder();
</code></pre>
<p>Below you can see all the available options.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr><th>No</th><th>Option</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>5.1.1</td><td><strong><code>.userId(String)</code></strong> <br> A =
unique identifier used to identify a user.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5.1.2</td><td><strong><code>.testMode(Boolean)</code></strong> <br>=
 Toggle Prodege SDK test mode.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5.1.3</td><td><strong><code>.userProperties(UserProperties)</code><=
/strong> <br> Provides user attributes upfront during initialization (only =
relevant with surveys).</td></tr>
<tr><td>5.1.4</td><td><strong><code>.advertisingOptOut(Boolean)</code></str=
ong> <br> Opts out from the use of the device's advertising identifier.</td=
></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><br></p>
<h3>5.1.1. <code>.userId(String)</code></h3>
<p>A unique identifier used to identify a user.</p>
<p>Setting the <code>userId</code> will override the default behaviour and =
use that instead of the Advertising Id in order to identify a user.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> <span style=3D"color: red">You can pass the id of=
 a user as identified on your system. Prodege will use this id to identify =
the user across sessions instead of an ad id/idfa as advised by the stores.=
 You are solely responsible for aligning with store regulations by providin=
g this id and getting relevant consent by the user when necessary. Prodege =
takes no responsibility for the usage of this id. In any request from your =
users on resetting/deleting this id and/or profile created, you should be s=
olely liable for those requests.</span></p>
</blockquote>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration: underline">Kotlin:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-kotlin hljs">optionsBuilder.userId(<span class=
=3D"hljs-string">"USER_ID"</span>)
</code></pre>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration: underline">Java:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-java hljs">optionsBuilder.userId(<span class=
=3D"hljs-string">"USER_ID"</span>);
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Failing to provide a user identifier and missing =
Google Play Advertising Identifier library will result to a failed initiali=
zation, unless you explicitly request for advertising opt out (section 5.1.=
4).</p>
</blockquote>
<p><br></p>
<h3>5.1.2. <code>.testMode(Boolean)</code></h3>
<p>Toggles the Prodege SDK Test mode.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong><code>true</code></strong> is used to show to the developer how=
 Prodege ads will be shown through an app (useful during development and te=
sting).</li>
<li><strong><code>false</code></strong> is the mode to be used for a releas=
ed app in any app store (start receiving paid surveys).</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> You should not be testing in live mode since your=
 account can get banned automatically from the system.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Prodege SDK runs by default in live mode. If you would like to test with=
 test ads:</p>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration:underline">Kotlin:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-kotlin hljs">optionsBuilder.testMode(<span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-literal">true</span>)
</code></pre>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration:underline">Java:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-java hljs">optionsBuilder.testMode(<span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">true</span>);
</code></pre>
<p><br></p>
<h3>5.1.3. <code>.userProperties(UserProperties)</code> (only relevant with=
 surveys)</h3>
<p>Provides user attributes upfront during initialization in order to skip =
or shorten Demographic surveys.</p>
<p>If you know upfront some user attributes like gender, age, education and=
 others you can pass them during initialization in order to shorten or skip=
 entirely Pollfish Demographic surveys and archieve better fill rate and hi=
gher priced surveys.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> You need to contact live support on our website t=
o request your account to be eligible for submitting demographic info throu=
gh your app, otherwise values submitted will be ignored by default.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> You can read more on demographic surveys along wi=
th a list with all the available options <a href=3D"https://www.pollfish.co=
m/docs/demographic-surveys" target=3D"_blank">here</a>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>An example of how you can create and pass a <code>UserProperties</code> =
object during initialization can be seen below:</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration: underline">Kotlin:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-kotlin hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">impo=
rt</span> com.prodege.builder.UserProperties

<span class=3D"hljs-variable"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">val</span> userP=
roperties</span> =3D UserProperties.Builder()
    .parentalStatus(UserProperties.ParentalStatus.TWO)
    .organizationRole(UserProperties.OrganizationRole.ADVERTISING)
    .numberOfEmployees(UserProperties.NumberOfEmployees.FIFTY_ONE_TO_HUNDRE=
ND)
    .educationLevel(UserProperties.EducationLevel.POST_GRADUATE)
    .career(UserProperties.Career.ADVERTISING)
    .income(UserProperties.Income.HIGH_I)
    .maritalStatus(UserProperties.MaritalStatus.SINGLE)
    .gender(UserProperties.Gender.MALE)
    .yearOfBirth(<span class=3D"hljs-number">1926</span>)
    .addSpokenLanguage(UserProperties.SpokenLanguage.GREEK)
    .addSpokenLanguage(UserProperties.SpokenLanguage.ENGLISH)
    .customAttribute(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"key"</span>, <span class=
=3D"hljs-string">"value"</span>)
    .build()

optionsBuilder.userProperties(userProperties)
</code></pre>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration: underline">Java:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-java hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import=
</span> com.prodege.builder.UserProperties;

UserProperties userProperties =3D <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">new</span> U=
serProperties.Builder()
    .parentalStatus(UserProperties.ParentalStatus.TWO)
    .organizationRole(UserProperties.OrganizationRole.ADVERTISING)
    .numberOfEmployees(UserProperties.NumberOfEmployees.FIFTY_ONE_TO_HUNDRE=
ND)
    .educationLevel(UserProperties.EducationLevel.POST_GRADUATE)
    .career(UserProperties.Career.ADVERTISING)
    .income(UserProperties.Income.HIGH_I)
    .maritalStatus(UserProperties.MaritalStatus.SINGLE)
    .gender(UserProperties.Gender.MALE)
    .yearOfBirth(<span class=3D"hljs-number">1926</span>)
    .addSpokenLanguage(UserProperties.SpokenLanguage.GREEK)
    .addSpokenLanguage(UserProperties.SpokenLanguage.ENGLISH)
    .customAttribute(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"key"</span>, <span class=
=3D"hljs-string">"value"</span>)
    .build();

optionsBuilder.userProperties(userProperties);
</code></pre>
<p><br></p>
<h3>5.1.4 <code>.advertisingOptOut(Boolean)</code></h3>
<p>Opts out from the use of the device's advertising identifier.</p>
<p>You can explicitly request to opt out from the use of the device's adver=
tising Id. This will configure Prodege SDK to use a unique session identifi=
er for each session. In case you skipped the Google Play Advertising Identi=
fier installation, you should set this option to <code>true</code> to avoid=
 initialization failure.</p>
<p>Providing a user identifier (section 5.1.1) will ignore the dependency o=
n the device advertising identifier and use that instead of a session ident=
ifier.</p>
<p>Prodege SDK runs by default in opt-in mode. If you would like to opt out=
:</p>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration:underline">Kotlin:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-kotlin hljs">optionsBuilder.advertisingOptOut(=
<span class=3D"hljs-literal">true</span>)
</code></pre>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration:underline">Java:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-java hljs">optionsBuilder.advertisingOptOut(<s=
pan class=3D"hljs-keyword">true</span>);
</code></pre>
<p><br></p>
<p>After configuring the <code>InitOptions.Builder</code> instance you can =
proceed with the build of the <code>InitOptions</code> object and Prodege S=
DK initialization.</p>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration:underline">Kotlin:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-kotlin hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">impo=
rt</span> com.prodege.Prodege

<span class=3D"hljs-variable"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">val</span> initO=
ptions</span> =3D optionsBuilder.build()

Prodege.initialize(context, <span class=3D"hljs-string">"API_KEY"</span>, l=
istener, initOptions)
</code></pre>
<p><span style=3D"text-decoration:underline">Java:</span></p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-java hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import=
</span> com.prodege.Prodege;

InitOptions initOptions =3D optionsBuilder.build();

Prodege.initialize(context, <span class=3D"hljs-string">"API_KEY"</span>, l=
istener, initOptions);
</code></pre>
<p><br></p>
<h3><strong>5.2. Listen for Prodege SDK initialization result (Optional)</s=
